{# Buyer / auction information pack (SPEC 12 step 6c), rebuilt to the team's own
   packs (docs/INFO-PACK-PLAYBOOK.md, derived from designs/incoming/DP2674,
   DP2777, DP2948.1 and DP2974).

   A4 **LANDSCAPE**, 297x210mm, white paper, black ink, the two brand golds
   (#ac874a mid, #ddc689 light). Every interior sheet carries the gold hairline
   frame, the grey/gold swoosh in the bottom-right corner and the black shield
   badge hung off the top-right. That furniture, the heavy uppercase titles and
   the black glyph beside every feature line are what make the document read as
   theirs rather than as a generic brochure.

   Page order (playbook 4):
     1. Cover                       white panel + full bleed photograph + circle
     2. Location details            MUST be page 2
     2b. Schedule of portions       multi-portion properties only
     3. Property features           one or more pages
     4. Gallery                     3x3, repeats until the photographs run out
     5. Investment highlights       MUST be second last
     6. Closing                     MUST be last
   A page with no data for it is omitted rather than printed empty.

   PAGE COMPOSITION IS MEASURED (D60, carried over from the portrait pack and
   re-derived for landscape). Blocks are costed in tenths of a millimetre; a list
   that is short for its sheet has its rows opened up, and what is STILL empty
   past FILL_MIN takes a photograph band that flexes into exactly the space left.

   Rendered from `public_view` only, so owner name/ID, occupant contact, bond and
   arrears are structurally absent (SPEC 4.4). No valuation figure appears: the
   municipal and professional valuations are stripped from the projection (D32,
   D54, D57) and the EVM range and comparable average are deliberately not
   printed either (playbook 11), so the money element is always the offers
   framing or the auction line. Monthly rates ARE shown, hedged: a running cost
   to the buyer, not a valuation of the property, and the reference packs print
   it.

   Auction vs sale is the key branch (playbook 7): auction and bidding words only
   when sale_process.method == "auction". A normal listing reads FOR SALE and
   uses offer language throughout. Figures are hedged, there are no em or en
   dashes, and the disclaimer is verbatim. #}
{% import "_adparts.html.j2" as parts %}

{% set is_auction = (vm.method == 'auction') %}
{% set pack_label = 'Auction information pack' if is_auction else 'Buyer information pack' %}

{# --- the method badge on the cover: first word gold, rest white, on black --- #}
{% set badge_lead = (vm.auction_channel or vm.auction_type or 'Liquidation') if is_auction else 'For' %}
{% set badge_tail = 'Auction' if is_auction else 'Sale' %}

{# --- the auction / viewing line printed large on the details page ---------- #}
{% set auction_bits = [] %}
{% if vm.auction_date %}{% set _ = auction_bits.append(vm.auction_date) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.auction_time %}{% set _ = auction_bits.append('@ ' ~ vm.auction_time) %}{% endif %}

{% set extent_str %}
{%- if vm.size_display %}± {{ vm.size_display }} m2{% if vm.size_ha %} (± {{ vm.size_ha }} ha){% endif %}{% endif -%}
{% endset %}

{# --- accommodation, in the words the pack reuses on the features list and the
   highlights table --------------------------------------------------------- #}
{% set accom = [] %}
{% if vm.beds %}{% set _ = accom.append(vm.beds ~ (' bedroom' if vm.beds == '1' else ' bedrooms')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.baths %}{% set _ = accom.append(vm.baths ~ (' bathroom' if vm.baths == '1' else ' bathrooms')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.separate_toilet %}{% set _ = accom.append('separate toilet') %}{% endif %}

{% set flatlet_line %}
{%- if vm.flatlet_beds %}{{ vm.flatlet_beds }} bedroom flatlet{% else %}Separate flatlet{% endif %}
{%- if vm.flatlet_features %} with {{ vm.flatlet_features | join(', ') | lower }}{% endif -%}
{% endset %}

{# --- photographs ---------------------------------------------------------- #}
{% set photos = vm.photos or [] %}
{% set hero = photos[0] if photos else None %}
{# The cover circle takes the second photograph so the sheet does not print the
   same picture twice; with one photograph it takes that one. #}
{% set circle_src = photos[1] if photos | length > 1 else hero %}
{% set gallery = photos[1:] if photos | length > 1 else [] %}
{% set gallery_pages = gallery | batch(9) | list %}
{# The closing page's ground, and the bands that fill short sheets. #}
{% set fill_photos = photos %}
{% set pool = namespace(i=0) %}

{# =========================================================================
   SHEET GEOMETRY, tenths of a millimetre, measured off the printed landscape
   A4: 210mm tall, 13mm top and 12mm bottom padding, and a title block of about
   20mm, leaving ~163mm of body.
   ========================================================================= #}
{% set REGION = 1630 %}
{% set FROW = 128 %}        {# one feature row: a 9mm glyph plus its padding #}
{% set FSUB = 38 %}         {# ... plus a sub line under the label #}
{% set COLHEAD = 92 %}      {# a gold column heading and its margin #}
{% set FOOTNOTE = 96 %}     {# the black footnote line under a features page #}
{% set CHIP = 100 %}        {# the complex-name chip in the bottom-right corner #}
{% set LINE = 46 %}         {# one line of 11px body text #}
{% set ROW_PAD = 22 %}      {# default padding on a feature row, per side #}
{% set TH_ROW = 62 %}       {# a table's heading row #}
{% set FILL_MIN = 260 %}    {# 26mm: past this a sheet reads as short, not spaced #}
{% set FILL_WIDE = 620 %}   {# past 62mm one photograph looks stretched: use two #}

{% macro padraw(budget, lines, rows, cap, base=ROW_PAD) %}{{ ([[(((budget - lines * FROW) // (2 * rows)) if rows else base), cap] | min, base] | max) }}{% endmacro %}

{# The band: photographs that take exactly the height a page has left over.
   flex-basis 0 and minmax(0, 1fr) rows mean it asks for no height of its own,
   so it can never be the block that pushes a sheet onto a second one. #}
{% macro fill_band(wide=false) -%}
{%- if fill_photos -%}
{%- set n = 2 if (wide and (fill_photos | length) > 1) else 1 -%}
  <div class="band" style="grid-template-columns: repeat({{ n }}, 1fr)">
    {%- for k in range(n) %}
    <img src="{{ fill_photos[(pool.i + k) % (fill_photos | length)] }}" alt="Property photograph">
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
{%- set pool.i = pool.i + n -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro %}

{# --- feature lists, costed --------------------------------------------- #}
{% set fm_all = vm.features_main or [] %}
{% set fc_all = vm.features_complex or [] %}

{% macro rowcost(items) %}{% set c = namespace(n=0) %}{% for f in items %}{% set c.n = c.n + FROW + (FSUB if split_label(f)[1] else 0) %}{% endfor %}{{ c.n }}{% endmacro %}

{# Two columns per sheet. The first features page also carries the footnote, so
   it holds slightly less than a continuation sheet. #}
{% set feat_budget = REGION - COLHEAD - FOOTNOTE %}
{% set feat_per_col = (feat_budget // FROW) %}
{% set feat_per_page = feat_per_col * 2 %}
{# The flatlet is a feature of the property, so it belongs in the list with a
   glyph beside it rather than buried in a footnote (the reference packs list
   "1-BED FLATLET" under external features). #}
{% set feat_all = fm_all + ([flatlet_line | trim] if vm.flatlet_present else []) + fc_all %}
{% set feat_pages = feat_all | batch(feat_per_page) | list %}

{# --- investment highlights: one row per fact the record actually holds ---- #}
{% set hl = [] %}
{% if is_auction %}
{% set _ = hl.append(('Offered on Auction', ((vm.auction_type ~ ' auction') if vm.auction_type else 'Auction') ~ (', ' ~ (auction_bits | join(' ')) if auction_bits else '') ~ '. The highest bid is subject to the seller\'s confirmation.')) %}
{% else %}
{% set _ = hl.append(('How It Is Offered', (vm.price_display or 'Offers invited') ~ ', subject to the conditions of sale and the seller\'s confirmation.')) %}
{% endif %}
{% if vm.location_line %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Established Location', vm.location_line ~ '.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if accom %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Practical Accommodation', (accom | join(', ')) | capitalize ~ ', as inspected.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.flatlet_present %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Separate Flatlet', (flatlet_line | trim) ~ ', offering potential for extended family, a work from home space or rental use.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if extent_str | trim %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Generous Extent', (extent_str | trim) ~ (', being the total of the ' ~ (vm.portions | length) ~ ' portions listed' if (vm.portions | length) > 1 else '') ~ ', to be confirmed on due diligence.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.garages and vm.garages != '0' %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Secure Parking', vm.garages ~ (' garage' if vm.garages == '1' else ' garages') ~ ' on the property.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.title_type_label %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Clean Title', vm.title_type_label ~ (', ' ~ vm.scheme if vm.scheme else '') ~ (' unit ' ~ vm.unit if vm.unit else '') ~ (', erf ' ~ vm.erf if vm.erf else '') ~ '.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.zoning %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Zoning', vm.zoning ~ ', to be confirmed on due diligence.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if fc_all %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Complex Facilities', (fc_all[:4] | join(', ')) ~ '.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if fm_all %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Main Residence', (fm_all[:3] | join('; ')) ~ '.')) %}{% endif %}
{% if vm.viewing_by_appt %}{% set _ = hl.append(('Viewing', 'Strictly by appointment through Dynamic Auctioneers.')) %}{% endif %}
{% set show_highlights = (hl | length) >= 5 %}
{% set hl_lines = namespace(n=0) %}
{% for label, detail in hl %}{% set hl_lines.n = hl_lines.n + 1 + ((detail | length) // 96) %}{% endfor %}

{# --- the tagline on the closing page, from the record's own words --------- #}
{% set close_lead %}
{%- if vm.descriptor_line %}{{ vm.descriptor_line }}{% if vm.suburb %} in {{ vm.suburb }}{% endif %}.
{%- else %}{{ vm.headline }}.{% endif -%}
{% endset %}

{# ========================================================================= #}
{% macro frame() %}<div class="frame"></div>{% endmacro %}

{% macro swoosh() %}
  <svg class="swoosh" viewBox="0 0 600 240" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
    <path d="M0 196c120-8 190-56 320-70 96-10 190 4 280 34v80H0z" fill="#d7d7d7"/>
    <path d="M96 240c76-58 152-96 268-104 92-6 168 8 236 34v70z" fill="#e8dece"/>
    <path d="M300 240c56-34 118-52 200-54 40 0 74 4 100 12v42z" fill="#cfcfcf"/>
  </svg>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro shield() %}
  <div class="shield">{{ parts.brand_logo(vm, 'dark', 'auctioneers') }}</div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro page_title(text) %}
  <h2 class="ptitle">{{ text }}</h2>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro pill(text, outline=false) %}
  <div class="pill {{ 'pill--out' if outline else '' }}">{{ text }}</div>
{% endmacro %}

{# One feature line: glyph, bold label, optional qualifier under it. #}
{% macro frow(text, pad='') %}
  {% set parts_ = split_label(text) %}
  <div class="frow"{% if pad %} style="--frowpad: {{ pad }}"{% endif %}>
    <span class="g">{{ glyph(icon_for(text)) }}</span>
    <span class="t">{{ parts_[0] }}{% if parts_[1] %}<span class="s">{{ parts_[1] }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro chip(icon, label, value) %}
  <div class="chip">
    <span class="ring">{{ glyph(icon, '7mm') }}</span>
    <span><b>{{ label }}</b><br>{{ value }}</span>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro fact(label, value) %}
  {% if value %}<div class="fact"><b>{{ label }}:</b> {{ value }}</div>{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ pack_label }} | {{ vm.headline }} | {{ vm.brand_name }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    /* Playbook 2, sampled off the vector reference pack. */
    --paper: #ffffff;
    --ink: #000000;
    --ink-2: #3f3f3f;
    --gold: #ac874a;
    --gold-2: #ddc689;
    --grey: #d7d7d7;
    --font: 'Montserrat', 'Avenir Next', 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;
  }
  @page { size: A4 landscape; margin: 0; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html {
    background: var(--paper);
    -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact;
  }
  body {
    margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
    font-family: var(--font); font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.5;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  img { max-width: 100%; }

  /* One physical A4 sheet, landscape. Fixed height, not min-height: the design
     is composed to the sheet, and a block that would overrun is clipped rather
     than allowed to spill a ragged extra page into the middle of the pack. */
  .page {
    position: relative; width: 297mm; height: 210mm; padding: 13mm 15mm 12mm;
    background: var(--paper); overflow: hidden;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    page-break-after: always; break-after: page;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; break-after: auto; }
  .page__body { position: relative; z-index: 2; flex: 1 1 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; }

  /* Furniture: gold hairline frame, corner swoosh, shield badge. */
  .frame {
    position: absolute; inset: 5mm; border: 1px solid var(--gold);
    border-radius: 4mm; z-index: 1; pointer-events: none;
  }
  .swoosh { position: absolute; right: 0; bottom: 0; width: 62%; height: 34%; z-index: 0; }
  .shield {
    position: absolute; top: 0; right: 16mm; width: 34mm; padding: 4mm 4mm 8mm;
    background: var(--ink); z-index: 3;
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 100% 74%, 50% 100%, 0 74%);
  }
  .shield img { width: 100%; display: block; }

  /* Titles: heavy uppercase with the pack's gold ghost offset. */
  .ptitle {
    margin: 0 0 5mm; font-size: 27px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .005em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink);
    text-shadow: .7mm .7mm 0 var(--gold-2);
  }
  .ptitle--mid { text-align: center; }
  .colhead {
    margin: 0 0 3mm; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .06em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); text-shadow: .5mm .5mm 0 rgba(0,0,0,.10);
  }

  /* --- cover ------------------------------------------------------------ */
  .cover { padding: 0; }
  .cover-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 0; background: #1a1a1a; }
  .cover-bg img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
  .cover-panel {
    position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: 22mm; width: 124mm; z-index: 2;
    background: #fff; overflow: hidden;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    padding: 14mm 10mm; text-align: center;
  }
  /* Explicit width/height rather than inset: an SVG sized only by offsets keeps
     its intrinsic ratio through the print path and prints a stamp of chevrons
     at the top instead of a ground behind the whole panel. */
  .chevrons { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; z-index: 0; opacity: .5; }
  .cover-panel > * { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .cover-logo { width: 66mm; margin-bottom: 13mm; }
  .cover-logo img { width: 100%; display: block; }
  .cover-desc {
    font-size: 31px; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.1; text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: -.015em;
  }
  .cover-desc--long { font-size: 24px; }
  .cover-place { margin-top: 1.5mm; font-size: 31px; font-weight: 900; line-height: 1.1; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); }
  .cover-city { margin-top: 1.5mm; font-size: 27px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .cover-badge {
    margin-top: 12mm; background: var(--ink); padding: 2.8mm 6mm;
    font-size: 21px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: .02em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #fff;
  }
  .cover-badge b { color: var(--gold-2); font-weight: 900; }
  .cover-ref {
    margin-top: 5mm; font-size: 9px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .18em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: #8a8a8a;
  }
  /* Positioned with plain offsets, not a transform: a transformed clipping box
     rasterises unreliably through the print path (the ring lost its bottom arc). */
  .cover-circle {
    position: absolute; z-index: 2; top: 44mm; left: 160mm;
    width: 122mm; height: 122mm; border-radius: 50%; overflow: hidden;
    border: 1.4mm solid var(--gold-2); background: #fff;
  }
  .cover-circle img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; border-radius: 50%; }

  /* --- location details -------------------------------------------------- */
  .ld { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr; gap: 6mm 10mm; flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; }
  /* The left column's blocks spread over the sheet rather than stacking at the
     top and leaving the foot empty; the facts stay put, the pills and the terms
     box take the slack between them. */
  .ld-left { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: space-between; min-height: 0; }
  .ld-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4mm 8mm; }
  .fact { font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .fact b { font-weight: 800; }
  .fact-group { margin-bottom: 3mm; }
  .chips { display: flex; gap: 10mm; margin: 4mm 0 3mm; }
  .chip { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 3mm; font-size: 11px; }
  .chip b { font-weight: 800; }
  .ring {
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 11mm; height: 11mm; border: 1.2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 50%; flex: 0 0 auto;
  }
  .pill {
    margin: 2.5mm 0; padding: 2.4mm 6mm; border-radius: 999px; text-align: center;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #cba869, #ac874a);
    color: var(--ink); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .04em;
  }
  .pill--out { background: #fff; border: 1.4px solid var(--gold); font-weight: 800; }
  .terms {
    border: 1.4px solid var(--ink); padding: 3.5mm 5mm; text-align: center;
    font-size: 10.5px; line-height: 1.85;
  }
  .terms b { font-weight: 800; }
  .ld-when {
    text-align: center; font-size: 21px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase;
    line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 4mm;
  }
  .ld-when small { display: block; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .ld-map { flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; border: 1.4px solid var(--gold); overflow: hidden; }
  .ld-map img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
  .ld-right { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; }

  /* --- features ---------------------------------------------------------- */
  .cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 4mm 12mm; flex: 1 1 auto; min-height: 0; }
  .cols > div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; }
  /* Rows spread down the sheet rather than stacking at the top: that is how the
     reference packs sit a four line feature list on a whole A4, and it fills a
     short page without any measurement at all. */
  .cols--spread > div { justify-content: space-between; }
  .cols--rule > div:first-child { border-right: 1px solid var(--gold); padding-right: 10mm; }
  .frow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5mm; padding: var(--frowpad, 2.2mm) 0; }
  .frow .g { flex: 0 0 auto; width: 9mm; height: 9mm; color: var(--ink); display: flex; }
  .frow .t {
    font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .01em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .frow .s {
    display: block; margin-top: .6mm; font-size: 8.5px; font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: .04em; color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  .boxgroup { border: 1.2px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 3mm; padding: 3mm 4mm; margin-bottom: 3mm; }
  .footline {
    margin-top: 4mm; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .06em;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink);
  }
  .chip-place {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 2.5mm; align-self: flex-end;
    border: 1.4px solid var(--gold); border-radius: 999px; padding: 2mm 5mm;
    font-size: 11px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em;
  }
  .chip-place svg { width: 4.5mm; height: 4.5mm; }

  /* --- gallery ----------------------------------------------------------- */
  .gal-head { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6mm; margin-bottom: 4mm; }
  .gal-badge { width: 34mm; background: var(--ink); padding: 3mm; }
  .gal-badge img { width: 100%; display: block; }
  /* Six tracks, not three: a photograph normally spans two of them, and the
     last row's photographs share the six between them, so a gallery of four or
     five never prints a row with an empty cell in it. */
  .grid3 {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); grid-auto-rows: minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 4mm; flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 0;
  }
  .grid3 img { width: 100%; height: 100%; min-height: 0; object-fit: cover; display: block; border: 1.2px solid var(--gold); }

  /* --- highlights -------------------------------------------------------- */
  .hl { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 10.5px; }
  .hl td { border: 1px solid #222; padding: var(--hlrow, 2.4mm) 3.5mm; vertical-align: middle; }
  .hl td:first-child { width: 27%; font-weight: 800; }

  /* --- closing ----------------------------------------------------------- */
  .close { padding: 0; }
  .close-bg { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 0; background: #14120f; }
  .close-bg img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; opacity: .5; }
  /* A dimming wash over the photograph, heavier at the foot where the contact
     rows and the disclaimer sit: white type on an undimmed photograph is what
     makes a closing page unreadable. */
  .close-bg::after {
    content: ''; position: absolute; inset: 0;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,0,0,.55) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,.42) 38%, rgba(0,0,0,.78) 100%);
  }
  .close-body {
    position: relative; z-index: 2; flex: 1 1 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    padding: 18mm 20mm 10mm; color: #fff;
  }
  .close-lead { border-left: 1.2mm solid var(--gold-2); padding-left: 6mm; max-width: 170mm; }
  .close-lead .a { font-size: 18px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .02em; line-height: 1.3; }
  .close-lead .b { margin-top: 2mm; font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; }
  .contacts { margin-top: auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4mm; }
  .crow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5mm; font-size: 15px; }
  .crow .ring { width: 11mm; height: 11mm; border-color: #fff; color: #fff; }
  .disclaimer {
    position: relative; z-index: 2; padding: 0 14mm 6mm; text-align: center;
    font-size: 7px; line-height: 1.55; font-weight: 600; color: #fff;
  }

  /* Bands fill a sheet that still runs short (D60). */
  .band {
    flex: 1 1 0; min-height: 0; margin-top: 5mm;
    display: grid; grid-auto-rows: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 4mm; overflow: hidden;
  }
  .band img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%; min-height: 0; object-fit: cover;
    display: block; border: 1.2px solid var(--gold);
  }

  /* On screen (gate 2 preview) the sheets sit on a ground so the pagination is
     visible; the printed PDF keeps the paper edge to edge. */
  @media screen {
    body { background: #e7e1d3; padding: 8mm 0; }
    .page { margin: 0 auto 8mm; box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.14), 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.16); }
  }
  @media print { .page { margin: 0; box-shadow: none; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  {# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1 COVER #}
  <section class="page cover">
    <div class="cover-bg">
      {% if hero %}<img src="{{ hero }}" alt="{{ vm.headline }}">{% endif %}
    </div>

    <div class="cover-panel">
      {# The panel's faint chevron ground. Drawn rather than tiled so it scales
         with the panel and prints without a background-image round trip. #}
      <svg class="chevrons" viewBox="0 0 124 210" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true">
        {% for i in range(-1, 8) %}
        <path d="M-14 {{ i * 30 }} L62 {{ i * 30 + 34 }} L138 {{ i * 30 }}" fill="none" stroke="#f2f2f2" stroke-width="11"/>
        {% endfor %}
      </svg>
      <div class="cover-logo">{{ parts.brand_logo(vm, 'light', 'auctioneers') }}</div>
      {% if vm.descriptor_line %}
      <div class="cover-desc {{ 'cover-desc--long' if vm.descriptor_line | length > 28 else '' }}">{{ vm.descriptor_line }}</div>
      {% else %}
      <div class="cover-desc cover-desc--long">{{ vm.headline }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if vm.suburb %}<div class="cover-place">{{ vm.suburb }}</div>{% endif %}
      {% if vm.municipality or vm.province %}
      <div class="cover-city">{{ vm.municipality or vm.province }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      <div class="cover-badge"><b>{{ badge_lead }}</b> {{ badge_tail }}</div>
      <div class="cover-ref">Property ref: {{ vm.property_ref }}</div>
    </div>

    {% if circle_src %}
    <div class="cover-circle"><img src="{{ circle_src }}" alt="{{ vm.headline }}"></div>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  {# ------------------------------------------------- 2 LOCATION DETAILS #}
  <section class="page">
    {{ swoosh() }}{{ frame() }}{{ shield() }}
    <div class="page__body">
      {{ page_title('Location details') }}

      <div class="ld">
        <div class="ld-left">
          <div class="ld-facts">
            <div>
              <div class="fact-group">
                <div class="fact"><b>Physical Address:</b></div>
                {% if vm.address %}<div class="fact">{{ vm.address }}</div>{% endif %}
                {% if vm.suburb %}<div class="fact">{{ vm.suburb }}</div>{% endif %}
                {% if vm.province %}<div class="fact">{{ vm.province }}</div>{% endif %}
              </div>
              {{ fact('Zoning', vm.zoning) }}
              {{ fact('Extent', extent_str | trim) }}
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="fact-group">
                <div class="fact"><b>Legal Address:</b></div>
                {% if vm.legal_description %}<div class="fact">{{ vm.legal_description }}</div>{% endif %}
                {% if vm.scheme %}<div class="fact">Scheme: {{ vm.scheme }}{% if vm.unit %}, unit {{ vm.unit }}{% endif %}</div>{% endif %}
                {% if vm.erf %}<div class="fact">Erf {{ vm.erf }}</div>{% endif %}
                {% if vm.title_deed_no %}<div class="fact">Title deed: {{ vm.title_deed_no }}</div>{% endif %}
              </div>
              {{ fact('Mun', vm.municipality) }}
              {{ fact('Title type', vm.title_type_label) }}
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="chips">
            {{ chip('doc', 'Rates & Taxes:', ('± R' ~ vm.monthly_rates) if vm.monthly_rates else 'TBC') }}
            {{ chip('doc', 'Levies:', 'TBC') }}
          </div>

          {{ pill('All Outstanding Fees, if any, to be Settled by the Seller.') }}

          {% if vm.terms %}
          <div class="terms">
            {% for t in vm.terms %}<div>{{ t }}</div>{% endfor %}
          </div>
          {% endif %}

          {{ pill('Subject To 30 days Confirmation By Seller') }}
        </div>

        <div class="ld-right">
          {% if is_auction %}
          <div class="ld-when">
            {{ (vm.auction_channel ~ ' auction') if vm.auction_channel else 'Auction' }}
            <small>{{ auction_bits | join(' ') if auction_bits else 'Date to be confirmed' }}</small>
          </div>
          {% else %}
          <div class="ld-when">
            Viewing:
            <small>{{ 'Strictly by appointment' if vm.viewing_by_appt else 'By arrangement with Dynamic Auctioneers' }}</small>
          </div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if vm.gps_str %}
          <div class="fact" style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:3mm">Coordinates: approx. {{ vm.gps_str }}</div>
          {% endif %}
          {% if photos %}
          <div class="ld-map"><img src="{{ photos[-1] }}" alt="{{ vm.headline }}"></div>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {# --------------------------------- 2b SCHEDULE OF PORTIONS (if any) #}
  {% if vm.portions %}
  {# Split EVENLY: twelve rows to a sheet is the cap, but 23 portions go 12 and
     11 rather than 12, 11 and then a page holding one orphan row. #}
  {% set sch_n = (((vm.portions | length) + 11) // 12) %}
  {% set sch_pages = vm.portions | batch((((vm.portions | length) + sch_n - 1) // sch_n)) | list %}
  {% for chunk in sch_pages %}
  {% set sch_rows = (chunk | length) + 1 + (1 if (loop.last and (vm.portions | length) > 1) else 0) %}
  {% set sch_pad = ([[((REGION - sch_rows * LINE) // (2 * sch_rows)), 110] | min, 24] | max) %}
  {% set sch_left = REGION - sch_rows * (LINE + 2 * sch_pad) %}
  {% set sch_band = fill_photos and sch_left >= FILL_MIN %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ swoosh() }}{{ frame() }}{{ shield() }}
    <div class="page__body">
      {{ page_title('Schedule of portions' if loop.first else 'Schedule of portions continued') }}
      <table class="hl sched" style="--hlrow: {{ sch_pad / 10 }}mm">
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Portion</td><td>Extent</td>{% if vm.portions | selectattr('deed') | list %}<td>Title deed</td>{% endif %}
          </tr>
          {% for p in chunk %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ p.label or 'Portion ' ~ loop.index }}{% if p.erf %} (erf {{ p.erf }}){% endif %}</td>
            <td>{% if p.size_display %}± {{ p.size_display }} m2{% endif %}</td>
            {% if vm.portions | selectattr('deed') | list %}<td>{{ p.deed or '' }}</td>{% endif %}
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
          {% if loop.last and vm.size_display and (vm.portions | length) > 1 %}
          <tr><td><b>Total extent</b></td><td><b>{{ extent_str | trim }}</b></td>{% if vm.portions | selectattr('deed') | list %}<td></td>{% endif %}</tr>
          {% endif %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      {% if sch_band %}{{ fill_band(sch_left >= FILL_WIDE) }}{% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}
  {% endif %}

  {# --------------------------------------------------- 3 PROPERTY FEATURES #}
  {% for chunk in feat_pages %}
  {% set half = (chunk | length + 1) // 2 %}
  {% set left = chunk[:half] %}
  {% set right = chunk[half:] %}
  {# What the taller of the two columns costs at default padding, then how much
     padding the sheet can afford, then what is STILL empty after that. Costed
     per column because the two sit side by side: the page is as tall as the
     taller one, never as tall as both. #}
  {% set rows = [left | length, right | length] | max %}
  {% set base_cost = [rowcost(left) | int, rowcost(right) | int] | max %}
  {% set budget = REGION - COLHEAD - (FOOTNOTE if loop.first else 0) - (CHIP if (loop.first and vm.scheme) else 0) %}
  {% set pad = ([[((budget - base_cost) // (2 * rows)) if rows else ROW_PAD, 70] | min, ROW_PAD] | max) %}
  {% set feat_left = budget - base_cost - rows * 2 * (pad - ROW_PAD) %}
  {# A sheet with room to spare spreads its rows over it. Only a genuinely short
     list - one that would leave a hand's width of paper even spread out - takes
     a photograph band instead, because rows that far apart stop reading as a
     list. #}
  {% set feat_band = fill_photos and feat_left >= FILL_WIDE %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ swoosh() }}{{ frame() }}{{ shield() }}
    <div class="page__body">
      {{ page_title('Property features' if loop.first else 'Property features continued') }}
      <div class="cols cols--rule {{ '' if feat_band else 'cols--spread' }}">
        <div>
          {% if loop.first %}<h3 class="colhead">{{ 'Main house:' if fm_all else 'Features:' }}</h3>{% endif %}
          {% for f in left %}{{ frow(f, (pad / 10) ~ 'mm') }}{% endfor %}
        </div>
        <div>
          {% if loop.first %}<h3 class="colhead">{{ 'External and shared:' if fc_all else 'Also included:' }}</h3>{% endif %}
          {% for f in right %}{{ frow(f, (pad / 10) ~ 'mm') }}{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
      {% if feat_band %}{{ fill_band(feat_left >= FILL_WIDE) }}{% endif %}
      {% if loop.first %}
      <div class="footline">Accommodation as inspected - all sizes and finishes to be confirmed on due diligence</div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if loop.first and vm.scheme %}
      <div class="chip-place">{{ glyph('pin', '4.5mm') }} {{ vm.scheme }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  {# ------------------------------------------------------------ 4 GALLERY #}
  {% for chunk in gallery_pages %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ swoosh() }}{{ frame() }}
    <div class="page__body">
      <div class="gal-head">
        <div class="gal-badge">{{ parts.brand_logo(vm, 'dark', 'auctioneers') }}</div>
        <h2 class="ptitle" style="margin:0">Gallery</h2>
      </div>
      {# Columns follow the count: two for a short gallery, three once there are
         five or more. The trailing part-row shares the six tracks equally. #}
      {% set cols = 1 if (chunk | length) == 1 else (2 if (chunk | length) <= 4 else 3) %}
      {% set full = (chunk | length) // cols * cols %}
      {% set rest = (chunk | length) - full %}
      <div class="grid3">
        {% for src in chunk %}
        <img src="{{ src }}" alt="Property photograph"
             style="grid-column: span {{ (6 // cols) if loop.index0 < full else (6 // rest) }}">
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  {# ------------------------------------- 5 INVESTMENT HIGHLIGHTS (2nd last) #}
  {% if show_highlights %}
  <section class="page">
    {{ swoosh() }}{{ frame() }}
    <div class="page__body">
      {{ page_title('Investment highlights') }}
      {# Row padding opened up so the table fills the sheet: the space left over
         once the text is laid out is divided over the rows rather than left as
         a hole under the last one. Costed on wrapped lines, capped at 9mm. #}
      {% set hl_pad = ([[((REGION - hl_lines.n * LINE) // (2 * (hl | length))) if hl else 24, 110] | min, 24] | max) %}
      <table class="hl" style="--hlrow: {{ hl_pad / 10 }}mm">
        <tbody>
          {% for label, detail in hl %}
          <tr><td>{{ label }}</td><td>{{ detail }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {# --------------------------------------------------------- 6 CLOSING #}
  <section class="page close">
    <div class="close-bg">
      {% if photos %}<img src="{{ photos[0] }}" alt="{{ vm.headline }}">{% endif %}
    </div>
    {{ frame() }}{{ shield() }}
    <div class="close-body">
      <div class="close-lead">
        <div class="a">{{ close_lead | trim }}</div>
        {# Literal template text, not an expression: an apostrophe inside a Jinja
           string is autoescaped to an entity, which is fine on the page but is
           not what a reader of the source (or a test) sees. #}
        <div class="b">{% if is_auction %}Don't miss this auction!{% else %}Enquiries and offers welcome.{% endif %}</div>
      </div>
      <div class="contacts">
        <div class="crow"><span class="ring">{{ glyph('pin', '6mm') }}</span>{{ vm.brand_address }}</div>
        <div class="crow"><span class="ring">{{ glyph('globe', '6mm') }}</span>{{ vm.brand_web }}</div>
        <div class="crow"><span class="ring">{{ glyph('mail', '6mm') }}</span>{{ vm.brand_email }}</div>
        <div class="crow"><span class="ring">{{ glyph('phone', '6mm') }}</span>{{ vm.brand_phone }}</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="disclaimer">
      Whilst all reasonable care has been taken to provide accurate information, neither Dynamic Solutions 1068 (Pty) LTD Trading As Dynamic Auctioneers nor the Seller/s guarantee the correctness of the information provided herein and neither will be held liable for any direct or indirect damages or loss, of whatsoever nature, suffered by any person as a result of errors or omissions in the information provided, whether due to negligence or otherwise of Dynamic Solutions 1068 (Pty) LTD Trading As Dynamic Auctioneers or the Seller/s or any other person.
    </div>
  </section>

</body>
</html>
